Phasmid: WebAuthn platform authenticator

What:     isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() and
          getClientCapabilities() userVerifyingPlatformAuthenticator report
          the profile's claim through the override Chrome uses for Google
          Password Manager passkeys; a ceremony finds no passkey. Guest
          sessions and the testing API behave as stock, and a Linux profile
          reports false on google.com, as Linux Chrome does. A Windows
          profile enables Secure Payment Confirmation in every process.
Why:      Windows Chrome reports Windows Hello and enables Secure Payment
          Confirmation by default; this build answers false on Linux.
Profile:  webauthn.user_verifying_platform_authenticator, os.family
Hooks:    chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc
          ChromeWebAuthenticationDelegate::
          IsUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailableOverride;
          chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc
          RegisterFeatureOverrides; chrome/browser/webauthn/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe; workers have no PublicKeyCredential
Guard:    tests/guards/core/profile-loading.py

